Krzys' writes:
 > 
 > The continued existence of stupid people can be explained by their
 > mothers' love. And I am not kidding. Think about it. Not just the
 > mother, of course, but I think there is something to it.

I wonder, too, how strongly intelligence *is* selected for.  Consider:

1.  Some never survive the hormone jangle of adolescence, culled by drunken
accidents or wild stunts gone wrong.  Over time stupid behavior is bound to
be fatal - longevity may be an indicator of luck or intelligence.  If we
reproduce at a young age (before misadventure strikes) smarts won't be a
selector.

2.  Is there any strong correlation between education and intelligence?  The
educated are simply not reproducing at the rate of the uneducated.  Concern
with careers and the "population bomb" engender reproductive responsibility.

3.  Perhaps very high intelligence is simply a case of diminishing returns in
terms of survival.  Intelligence is obviously our trump in terms of survival,
but moronic intelligence may be sufficient for interspecies competition.  That
would still allow hunting, agriculture, etc.

Suppose we were to slip over the precipice into nuclear annihilation - or
what if we're done in by a nanotech hacker.  Would our epitaph be:

  They were too smart for their own good.
  
  or

  When push came to shove, they weren't smart enough.


Sorry for the dynamic pessimism, but the spirit of intellectual inquiry
compels...


